Global Exception Handling :
Global Exception Handling is a mechanism that catches exceptions (errors) occurring anywhere in your application 
and handles them from a single centralized class.

| Annotation          | Purpose                                  |
| ------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| `@ControllerAdvice` | Makes a class a global exception handler |
| `@ExceptionHandler` | Handles specific exceptions              |
| `@ResponseStatus`   | Sets HTTP status code                    |
| `ResponseEntity`    | Returns custom response                  |

@JacksonXmlRootElement : It is a Jackson XML annotation used to specify the root element name of an 
XML document when converting a Java object to XML.
Syntax : @JacksonXmlRootElement(localName = "studentDetails")
//localName → Name of the root XML tag.
